BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Congregation Shomrei Emunah
UID:TU2006148638
DTSTAMP:20261029T000314Z
SUMMARY:Midday MeetUp - Blueberries\, New Jersey’s Wonder Fruit
DESCRIPTION:**Midday MeetUp - Blueberries\, New Jersey’s Wonder Fruit**  
  \nA monthly gathering to make connections and learn together.  \n11:45am 
 Catered Lunch (free)  \n12:30pm  Featured Program   \n  \nSpeaker: Food 
 historian\, Judith Krall-Russo  \n  \nThe cultivated blueberry has its roo
 ts in the Pinelands of New Jersey.  Elizabeth White along with Dr. Fredri
 ck Coville\, proved that the “swamp huckleberry” could be cultivated. 
 Learn the history of this fascinating berry and the contributions Elizabet
 h White of Whitesbog made to their cultivation. Today the blueberry is tou
 ted as the wonder fruit with a host of healthful benefits.  Learn about t
 he history\, health benefits and a variety of ways to prepare and savor th
 ese berries.  \n  \n**Cost:** FREE or Suggested Donation of $10 per person
  to offset costs. (Bill My Account is only open to Shomrei Members)  \n  \
 n**RSVP:** Required so we know how much food to buy.  \nhttps://shomrei.ea
 syshul.com/events/6967e4b6368f110026c0c460  \n  \n**\\***Members &amp\; Pr
 eSchool Families should use their fob to access the building.   \n  \nFull
 _Season_Schedule_for_Midday_MeetUps: https://shomrei.org/calendar/midday-m
 eetup-calendar  \n  \n**Questions?** Contact June Zimmerman\,   \nVP for P
 rogramming  \njzimmerman@shomrei.org  \n  \n\\#middaymeetup\n\n
LOCATION:Social Hall
CATEGORIES:Events
CLASS:PUBLIC
TRANSP:OPAQUE
SEQUENCE:0
