BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Congregation Shomrei Emunah
UID:TU2007101531
DTSTAMP:20261029T000314Z
SUMMARY:Midday MeetUp - Bonnie Rapp\, Best of Broadway
DESCRIPTION:**Midday MeetUp - Bonnie Rapp\, Best of Broadway   \nA monthly
  gathering to make connections and learn together.  \n11:45am Catered Lunc
 h (free)  \n12:30pm  Featured Program   \n  \nExperience *The Best of B
 roadway* as Bonnie Rapp brings to life unforgettable moments from Tony Aw
 ard–winning musicals. Relive the golden age of musical theatre through 
 beloved classics and timeless melodies by legendary composers such as Rodg
 ers and Hammerstein\, Lerner and Loewe\, Frank Loesser\, Irving Berlin and
  more!  \n  \nCost:** FREE or Suggested Donation of $10 per person to off
 set costs. (Bill My Account is only open to Shomrei Members)  \n  \n**RSVP
 :** Required so we know how much food to buy.  \nhttps://shomrei.easyshul
 .com/events/6967e6f2368f110026c0c486  \n  \n**\\***Members &amp\; PreSchoo
 l Families should use their fob to access the building.  \n About Bonnie R
 app**  \nBonnie had the honor of performing the lead role of Christine Daa
 é in the National Tour/San Francisco Company of Andrew Lloyd Webber's The
  Phantom of the Opera. Some of Bonnie’s favorite roles include Maria in 
 The Sound of Music\, Kate in Kiss Me\, Kate\, Cinderella in Rodgers and Ha
 mmerstein’s Cinderella\, Louise in Gypsy and Sister Amnesia and Sister L
 eo in Nunsense\, Nunsense II and Nunsense Jamboree.  In addition\, Bonnie
  has appeared in numerous galas\, fundraisers\, and Broadway concerts\, in
 cluding performances at Lincoln Center's Avery Fisher Hall.  \n  \nFor the
  past decade\, Bonnie has devoted her talents to providing live musical en
 tertainment for a wide range of audiences\, including corporate and commun
 ity events\, libraries\, private celebrations\, JCCs\, and residents of in
 dependent living\, assisted living\, nursing homes\, and memory care commu
 nities.  \n  \nFull_Season_Schedule_for_Midday_MeetUps: https://shomrei.or
 g/calendar/midday-meetup-calendar  \n  \n**Questions?** Contact June Zimme
 rman\,   \nVP for Programming  \njzimmerman@shomrei.org  \n  \n\\#middayme
 etup\n\n
LOCATION:Social Hall
CATEGORIES:Events
CLASS:PUBLIC
TRANSP:OPAQUE
SEQUENCE:0
