UID:TU2131910341
DTSTAMP:20261029T000314Z
SUMMARY:Selichot - Service\, Dinner\, Music!
DESCRIPTION:Start the High Holidays with joy\, music and community! Join u
 s for a lively evening packed with delicious food\, soulful singing and sw
 eet treats. Connect with the Shomrei community over dinner and sing High H
 oliday melodies. Unwind with dessert and smooth sounds from our jazz band.
  It’s a celebration you won’t want to miss!\n\n**RSVP Required for Din
 ner and Reception** **http://shomrei.org/jazz**: http://shomrei.org/jazz\n
 \nFree or Suggested Donation:  \n$20 per adult\,  $10 per child over 12\,
   $36 per family\n\n**------------------------------  \nAdults and Kids 8
 + (Younger Kids/Scroll Down)**  \n6:30 Welcome   \n6:45 Dinner (Middle Ea
 stern dairy dinner)  \n8:00 Havdalah and Selichot Service  \n9:00 Dessert 
 and Jazz Reception\n\nAs Shabbat comes to a close\, children and adults wi
 ll come together to recite Havdalah prayers. We are looking forward to hav
 ing our children who are 8 yrs old and up help lead the havdalah candle li
 ghting ceremony while reciting prayers with Rabbi Julie.\n\nParticipatory\
 , music-filled service led by Rabbi Julie\, Talia Lakritz\, Suzanna Grobma
 n\, Debra Caplan and accompanied by Oren Neiman and his jazz ensemble.\n\n
 The party continues with a dessert reception. Live music will be provided 
 by the jazz ensemble.\n\n**Livestream:** http://shomrei.org/live\n\n**---
 ---------------------------**\n\n**Kids 7 and Younger**  \n6:30 Little Kid
 s' Dinner   \n7:00 Free Play  \n7:30 Selichot Inspired Art Activity  \n8:
 00 Children welcome to stay in childcare\, or join Selichot service\n\n**-
 -----------------------------**\n\n**Have questions? Want to Help out? Co
 ntact:** Shomrei Office  \noffice@shomrei.org  \n(973) 746-5031\n\n**What 
 is Selichot?**  \nThe Hebrew word selichah means “forgiveness.” The pl
 ural form of the word selichah is selichot\, a word traditionally used to 
 refer to additional prayers for forgiveness recited during the month of El
 ul (through Yom Kippur). We gather together on the Saturday night before R
 osh Hashanah to meditate on the capacity for forgiveness and on its power.
  In joining together\, we help each other pray for that blessing – to gi
 ve it and to receive it.\n\n
LOCATION:Social Hall\, Gallery\, [#]holiday:rosh_hashanah\, ~Extra Parking:
  73 & 77 Park St.\, Livestream
CATEGORIES:Events
CLASS:PUBLIC
TRANSP:OPAQUE
SEQUENCE:0
