UID:TU2178208084
DTSTAMP:20261029T000314Z
SUMMARY:Art Talk: Deborah Ugoretz
DESCRIPTION:https://deborahugoretz.com  \nIG:@debugoretz  \n@ketubah\\_for\
 \_life\n\nDeborah Ugoretz is a master paper-cutter with 40 years of experi
 ence facilitating workshops and classes on Jewish paåpercutting and Hebre
 w illuminated manuscripts. Deborah has shown her work in galleries and mus
 eums across New York City and the US\, and has served as a leader in artis
 t communities as a curator for Yiddish New York and organizer of Red Hook 
 Open Studios. In 2024\, she was awarded a Folk Arts Fellowship by NY Counc
 il on the Arts and the New York Foundation for the Arts.  \n  \nDeborah sh
 ares her skill as an educator\, most recently at the New School\, National
  Yiddish Book Center\, Yeshiva University Museum\, the Museum at Eldridge 
 Street\, New York and at Fordham University where a retrospective of her c
 ut paper work was exhibited. For eight years\, Deborah produced an Artist
  *Beit Midrash*\, a workshop where artists generate new work in dialogue w
 ith Jewish texts and scholarship. Deborah was also a mentor in the art of 
 Jewish papercutting through a grant from the New Jersey State Council for 
 the Arts.  \n  \nIn papercutting\, Deborah found a way to merge her work a
 s an artist and her Jewish heritage. “I began to search through texts\, 
 through the Bible and prayer for visual imagery\,” she said. “Through 
 that search\, I began to discover how rich and full these writings were. 
  I wanted to communicate that wealth by releasing the words\, through my a
 rt\, into pictorial space". Her interest in Jewish marriage contracts (*ke
 tubot*) led her to study Hebrew and English calligraphy and the art of ill
 uminated manuscripts.  \n  \nUgoretz creates work in cut paper for organiz
 ations and book covers\, Jewish marriage contracts. She also paints with a
 crylics and builds mobiles\, small scale boxes and screens in her studio i
 n Red Hook\, Brooklyn.\n\n
LOCATION:Gallery
CATEGORIES:Events
CLASS:PUBLIC
TRANSP:OPAQUE
SEQUENCE:0
