SUMMARY:From Swastika to Jim Crow: Screening and Discussion
DESCRIPTION:***From Swastika to Jim Crow*: Screening and Discussion**  \n  
 \nExplore an influential\, little-known chapter in the history of Black-Je
 wish relations in America. We'll be screening a documentary film\, From Sw
 astika to Jim Crow\,  based on a book by the same title by Gabrielle Simo
 n Edgcomb. It tells the story of German-Jewish refugees\, who\, expelled f
 rom their homeland by Hitler and the Nazis\, found new lives and careers a
 t historically Black colleges and universities in the American South\, inf
 luencing a whole generation of Black students and professionals.   \n  \n
 After the screening\, Dr. Lillie Johnson Edwards and Rabbi Julie will disc
 uss the film's significance.   \n  \nDr. Edwards is a Drew University Pro
 fessor Emerita of History and African American Studies.   \n  \nCo-sponso
 red by Shomrei &amp\; The_Mark: https://themarkmtc.org.\n\n
LOCATION:Montclair Public Library\, 50 S Fullerton Ave\, Montclair\, NJ 070
 42\, USA
CATEGORIES:Events
CLASS:PUBLIC
TRANSP:OPAQUE
SEQUENCE:0
